WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.908
<i>I think that</i>


00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:53.320
<i>actually everything I've experienced
over these last few months...</i>


00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:58.120
<i>is like being in a dream...</i>


00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.200
<i>...or in a movie.</i>


00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:07.228
<i>But a very bad movie,</i>


00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:11.840
<i>because that movie would be
very unrealistic.</i>


00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:20.988
<i>It's fashionable these days to
blame everything on global warming.</i>


00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.108
<i>Particularly on
man-made global warming.</i>


00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:26.428
<i>But I'm afraid the evidence
doesn't point in that direction.</i>


00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:29.348
<i>A little bit of warming
would not be a bad thing for myself,</i>


00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:30.908
<i>being a Canadian</i>


00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:32.948
<i>and the people in Russia
wouldn't mind a little...</i>


00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:35.228
<i>A couple of degrees warmer either.</i>


00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:38.948
<i>All of this with the
global warming, a lot of it's a hoax.</i>


00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:42.788
<i>It's a hoax, I mean, it's a money-making
industry, okay. It's a hoax.</i>


00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:45.268
<i>The whole
"climate crisis" as they call it,</i>


00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:48.188
<i>is not only fake news, it's fake science.</i>


00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:52.588
<i>There is no climate crisis.
There is nothing to be afraid of.</i>


00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.948
<i>How much warming will you get if you,</i>


00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.388
<i>let us say, double the CO2 in the air?</i>


00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.948
<i>The answer is,
you don't get very much.</i>


00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.028
<i>The problem is not global warming.</i>


00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:07.228
<i>The problem is that we
keep hearing one-sided arguments.</i>


00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:10.788
<i>Carbon dioxide is
actually a benefit to the environment,</i>


00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:15.228
<i>to agriculture and forestry,
and to the climate of the earth.</i>


00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:18.828
<i>There are some people
who are so arrogant to think</i>


00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:21.348
<i>that they are so powerful,
they can change climate.</i>


00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.880
<i>Man can't change climate.</i>


00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.108
<i>Adults always say one thing</i>


00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.680
<i>and then do something
completely different.</i>


00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:06.028
<i>They say that we only have one planet,</i>


00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.748
<i>and we should take care of it.</i>


00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:12.480
<i>And yet no one gives a damn
about the climate crisis.</i>


00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:19.720
<i>My name is Greta Thunberg,
and I am 15 years old.</i>


00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.428
<i>I am on a school strike for the climate
in front of the Parliament,</i>


00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:26.320
<i>until the election day.</i>


00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:27.348
<i>Many have heard about climate change</i>


00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:30.828
<i>and know vaguely what it means</i>


00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:34.868
<i>with rising sea levels,
increased average temperatures,</i>


00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:36.508
<i>and so on.</i>


00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:41.948
<i>But no one seems to
fully understand the consequences.</i>


00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:46.200
<i>That we are right now
living as if we had several Earths.</i>


00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:55.628
<i>Sometimes it feels like we
who have Asperger's or autism</i>


00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:58.520
<i>are the only ones
who see through the noise.</i>


00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:27.268
I am protesting about the climate crisis
because it's such an important issue.


00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:31.068
What we are doing now,
future generations can't change.


00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:33.588
And no one is doing anything,
nothing is happening.


00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:35.520
So I must do what I can.


00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:39.708
<i>What did you think
when you first heard her talking</i>


00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:41.708
<i>about the idea to start protesting?</i>


00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:45.828
<i>I told her if she would
do that, I would not support it.</i>


00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:51.880
So she made a very long list of facts
that she's been handing out to people.


00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:55.308
And, uh, she knows
the climate issue, I would say


00:06:55.320 --> 00:07:00.508
better than 97% of all the politicians,
probably in the world.


00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.788
She has almost a photographic memory


00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:04.828
when it comes
to things she's interested in.


00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:10.600
So she can read books and almost
remember everything that's in there.


00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:12.988
<i>Did you expect something like that?</i>


00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:15.228
<i>I didn't expect anything.</i>


00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:18.040
<i>I just wanted her to be happy.</i>


00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:21.268
<i>And I'm very sure that
she didn't expect anything either.</i>


00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:23.788
<i>I mean, she just...
She felt she had to do something</i>


00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:26.720
<i>and she had to do it
completely on her own.</i>


00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:36.948
<i>I don't like making small talk with people</i>


00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:39.720
<i>or socializing.</i>


00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:50.080
<i>Sometimes, I go quiet
and can stay so for hours</i>


00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:54.080
<i>only because I simply can't talk.</i>


00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:59.988
<i>I like to have routines,</i>


00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:04.080
<i>and I notice details.</i>


00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:08.908
<i>And once I really get
interested in something,</i>


00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:12.548
<i>I can get, like, laser focused on it</i>


00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:15.640
<i>and keep doing it for hours,
without getting bored.</i>


00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:38.560
<i>We saw a film in school.</i>


00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:45.228
<i>There were
starving polar bears, floodings,</i>


00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:47.400
<i>hurricanes and droughts.</i>


00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:57.348
<i>And the scientists said that
we didn't have much time left</i>


00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:59.200
<i>to change our behavior.</i>


00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:09.800
<i>That was when
I started getting depressed.</i>


00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:13.440
<i>And got anxiety.</i>


00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:20.040
<i>And stopped eating and stopped talking.</i>


00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:28.880
<i>I was sick.
I almost starved to death.</i>


00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:37.600
<i>It took many years</i>


00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:41.560
<i>but slowly.</i>


00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:45.720
<i>I started to feel better.</i>


00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:57.108
<i>I felt that,
why should I give up</i>


00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:59.788
<i>when there were so many different things</i>


00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:02.400
<i>you could do to make a difference?</i>


00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:36.308
"I love seeing someone
who doesn't just complain.


00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:39.268
"But gets out and does
something about it.


00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:40.480
You inspire me."


00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:25.908
<i>My name is Greta
Thunberg and I am 15 years old.</i>


00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:30.720
<i>And we have had school strikes
for the climate for three weeks.</i>


00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:38.388
<i>But we will go on with
the school strike every Friday.</i>


00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:42.628
<i>As from now, we will sit
