Thank you so
much for coming, Greta.


00:37:10.120 --> 00:37:14.668
Honestly, we would have
never started this if you wouldn't have.


00:37:14.680 --> 00:37:17.588
And I would have never
had the courage you showed.


00:37:17.600 --> 00:37:21.788
It's not that I should take the focus,
because that's what's so good


00:37:21.800 --> 00:37:25.428
about this movement,
that everyone is equally contributing.


00:37:25.440 --> 00:37:30.588
No, no, that's right, but everybody's
doing great jobs locally in every country.


00:37:30.600 --> 00:37:36.108
But you're, like,
that girl that started it all, you know?


00:37:36.120 --> 00:37:39.068
I think we needed
this kind of story that you told.


00:37:39.080 --> 00:37:41.908
Like a story of, like,
everyone can make a difference.


00:37:41.920 --> 00:37:45.068
And that we as young people
can change something.


00:37:45.080 --> 00:37:49.348
And we needed the story
to tell to other people and they saw it.


00:37:49.360 --> 00:37:52.988
- Yeah, it's really nice.
- Together we can make a difference.


00:37:53.000 --> 00:37:58.800
There have now been strikes
on every continent except Antarctica.


00:38:00.040 --> 00:38:04.988
I think that it's
amazing that it's not just in...


00:38:05.000 --> 00:38:07.628
Western Europe. It's everywhere.


00:38:10.360 --> 00:38:12.468
- What do we want?
- Climate justice!


00:38:12.480 --> 00:38:15.148
- When do we want it?
- Now!


00:38:18.520 --> 00:38:21.268
<i>I'm impressed by the political oomph</i>


00:38:21.280 --> 00:38:23.188
<i>that this movement seems to have got.</i>


00:38:23.200 --> 00:38:25.068
<i>Climate change has
never been on the headlines like this</i>


00:38:25.080 --> 00:38:27.428
<i>for as long as I can remember.</i>


00:38:27.440 --> 00:38:30.308
<i>It's really making people understand
that this needs to be tackled now.</i>


00:38:30.320 --> 00:38:33.720
<i>It is the most pressing
political issue of our time.</i>


00:38:34.560 --> 00:38:36.188
<i>Society is like an amoeba,</i>


00:38:36.200 --> 00:38:38.508
<i>it moves from the margins,
not from the center.</i>


00:38:38.520 --> 00:38:44.560
<i>If the young people can sustain this,
this actually could change the world.</i>


00:38:47.160 --> 00:38:52.148
Are you ready to meet Greta?


00:38:52.160 --> 00:38:55.520
Make some noise!


00:39:08.240 --> 00:39:10.428
This is incredible.


00:39:15.560 --> 00:39:18.188
For way too long,
the people in power


00:39:18.200 --> 00:39:22.388
have gotten away with not
caring about the climate crisis.


00:39:22.400 --> 00:39:26.188
But we will make sure
they will not do that any more.


00:39:26.200 --> 00:39:32.188
We will be a pain in the ass, we will
keep on striking until they do something.


00:39:32.200 --> 00:39:34.628
Everybody, raise your hands!


00:40:27.320 --> 00:40:29.828
- Hi, how are you?
- I'm good. You?


00:40:29.840 --> 00:40:32.348
- Nice meeting you.
- Nice meeting you too.


00:40:32.360 --> 00:40:35.708
It's an honor to meet you.
Thank you for inviting me.


00:40:35.720 --> 00:40:39.148
- You are welcome.
We are very happy to have you here.


00:40:39.160 --> 00:40:41.708
What I want to discuss with you is


00:40:41.720 --> 00:40:45.748
how you see the situation and on
which topic do you want us to focus?


00:40:45.760 --> 00:40:50.268
And what are your main
concerns and expectations?


00:40:50.280 --> 00:40:53.428
I think we are in a time now
where more and more people


00:40:53.440 --> 00:40:56.348
are becoming aware of what is going on.


00:40:56.360 --> 00:40:58.908
And I think we have
reached a tipping point.


00:40:58.920 --> 00:41:02.828
That people will...
Will demand things.


00:41:02.840 --> 00:41:07.108
And will realize where we are at.


00:41:07.120 --> 00:41:12.108
And I think that you have a great
opportunity to take that chance and to act


00:41:12.120 --> 00:41:14.908
and to become a figure of this.


00:41:14.920 --> 00:41:18.228
And also, I think it's
very important that we...


00:41:18.240 --> 00:41:24.028
In the rich countries,
we need to lead and to act more.


00:41:24.040 --> 00:41:26.508
Obviously, because
the people in poorer countries


00:41:26.520 --> 00:41:30.868
need to have a chance to
heighten their standard of living.


00:41:30.880 --> 00:41:33.748
So, you are in a rush,
so you should probably get going.


00:41:33.760 --> 00:41:35.600
Thank you very much. Thank you.


00:41:36.880 --> 00:41:39.508
How do you manage
everything for school and so on?


00:41:39.520 --> 00:41:42.108
I... my school is
actually very helpful.


00:41:42.120 --> 00:41:48.108
They support me and I do homework
at home and I catch up with them.


00:41:48.120 --> 00:41:50.748
I-I work hard.


00:41:50.760 --> 00:41:54.840
- Wow. And you travel a lot?
- Yeah. Sometimes. Yeah.


00:41:57.080 --> 00:42:00.828
- By train.
- Yeah. Yeah.


00:42:00.840 --> 00:42:04.068
Wow. And you
read a lot on the climate?


00:42:04.080 --> 00:42:07.988
Yeah, I do, yeah. A lot. I'm a nerd.


00:42:29.040 --> 00:42:34.988
- My name is Greta Thunberg.
I am a climate activist from Sweden.


00:42:35.000 --> 00:42:38.708
People always tell us
that they are so hopeful.


00:42:38.720 --> 00:42:43.108
They are hopeful that the young people
are going to save the world.


00:42:43.120 --> 00:42:47.908
But we are not.
There is simply not enough time


00:42:47.920 --> 00:42:51.868
to wait for us to grow up
and become the ones in charge.


00:42:51.880 --> 00:42:57.920
Because by the year 2020, we need to have
bent the emissions curve steeply downward.


00:42:58.520 --> 00:43:01.228
That is next year.


00:43:01.240 --> 00:43:04.188
We have started
to clean up your mess.


00:43:04.200 --> 00:43:08.388
And we will not stop
until we are done. Thank you.


00:43:16.640 --> 00:43:18.428
And now I have the pleasure and privilege


00:43:18.440 --> 00:43:20.880
of giving the floor
to Jean-Claude Juncker.


00:43:31.880 --> 00:43:34.548
<i>Now I'm going to really focus</i>


00:43:34.560 --> 00:43:37.828
<i>on what's happening here today.</i>


00:43:37.840 --> 00:43:43.308
<i>I change things...</i>


00:43:43.320 --> 00:43:47.268
<i>while trying to
regulate smaller things.</i>


00:43:47.280 --> 00:43:51.108
<i>Now, in terms of flushes,
they said that</i>


00:43:51.120 --> 00:43:54.840
<i>we need to harmonize all flushes
across all toilets in Europe.</i>


00:43:57.040 --> 00:44:02.400
<i>Well, it could be useful because we would
save a very large amount of energy, but...</i>


00:44:14.800 --> 00:44:18.548
<i>I honestly don't understand</i>


00:44:18.560 --> 00:44:20.240
<i>why I even get invited.</i>


00:44:22.840 --> 00:44:26.748
<i>It feels like all they
want is to be spotlighted</i>


00:44:26.760 --> 00:44:32.240
<i>to make it look like they care,
as if they were doing something.</i>


00:44:35.200 --> 00:44:40.828
<i>They know what to say,
they know what sells.</i>


00:44:40.840 --> 00:44:44.360
<i>But in fact,
they're doing basically nothing.</i>


00:44:47.640 --> 00:44:53.228
<i>If the solution to the climate crisis was
about changing tea bags for loose-leaf tea</i>


00:44:53.240 --> 00:44:58.388
<i>and eating vegetarian once a week,
then it wouldn't be a crisis.</i>


00:44:58.400 --> 00:45:01.240
<i>And we wouldn't even have a problem.</i>


00:45:02.880 --> 00:45:06.908
<i>Have you heard any
politicians seem to understand the urgency?</i>


00:45:06.920 --> 00:45:10.948
Today, President Juncker's
speech did not seem to respond to...


00:45:10.960 --> 00:45:14.388
You laid out even science facts
and he didn't even respond to those.


00:45:14.400 --> 00:45:18.668
No. I mean, um,
most people like that I talk to


00:45:18.680 --> 00:45:23.468
don't really respond, they don't
come with any concrete promises.


00:45:23.480 --> 00:45:27.880
They only say that we are trying,
but that's not enough.


00:45:47.280 --> 00:45:50.428
<i>If we don't act
now, the world will get so hot</i>


00:45:50.440 --> 00:45:52.508
<i>millions of people
will lose their homes</i>


00:45:52.520 --> 00:45:57.628
<i>and more than 10% of the world's insects,
plants and animals will die.</i>


00:45:57.640 --> 00:46:01.388
<i>Japan is experiencing
a record-breaking heat wave</i>


00:46:01.400 --> 00:46:05.028
<i>which officials say contributed
to the death of 65 people last week...</i>


00:46:05.040 --> 00:46:08.308
<i>The impact on sensitive
ecosystems and the Arctic</i>


00:46:08.320 --> 00:46:11.188
<i>will shift from high
to very high risk...</i>


00:46:11.200 --> 00:46:14.188
<i>Sixty-three fires are burning in 13 states</i>


00:46:14.200 --> 00:46:17.588
<i>and with dangerous heat coming,
the situation will only get worse...</i>


00:46:17.600 --> 00:46:19.748
<i>Now is the time to stop this.</i>


00:46:19.760 --> 00:46:22.640
<i>We don't have another decade to wait.</i>


00:47:10.760 --> 00:47:13.908
<i>Greta, I have just one
question for you. How does it feel?</i>


00:47:13.920 --> 00:47:16.428
<i>I don't know.
It's very overwhelming.</i>


00:47:16.440 --> 00:47:19.588
<i>Because they're here
for you. It's all because you started it.</i>


00:47:19.600 --> 00:47:23.748
<i>No, they're here for
themselves. And for everyone.</i>


00:47:46.120 --> 00:47:49.308
Greta, I think they love you
too much.


00:48:00.120 --> 00:48:02.120
Please, you're my hero.


00:48:17.520 --> 00:48:18.908
Thank you.


00:48:25.720 --> 00:48:28.228
Are you not hungry?


00:48:28.240 --> 00:48:32.388
- I don't care. No.
- You don't care?


00:48:32.400 --> 00:48:36.908
- Do you want to go elsewhere?
- No, I want to sit here and not eat.


00:48:36.920 --> 00:48:38.080
Okay.


00:52:53.040 --> 00:52:59.040
<i>Today, we use
100 million barrels of oil every day.</i>


00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:03.188
There are no
politics to change that.


00:53:03.200 --> 00:53:06.760
There are no rules
to keep that oil in the ground.


00:53:07.960 --> 00:53:13.268
But if being carbon-neutral
does not include transportation,


00:53:13.280 --> 00:53:17.788
shopping, food,
aviation and shipping


00:53:17.800 --> 00:53:19.908
then it doesn't
really mean that much.


00:53:24.760 --> 00:53:30.800
<i>Some would say we are wasting lesson time.
We say we are changing the world.</i>


00:53:31.480 --> 00:53:34.908
<i>So that when we are older,
we will be able to look back</i>


00:53:34.920 --> 00:53:37.028
<i>and say that we
did everything we could.</i>


00:53:37.040 --> 00:53:39.508
<i>And we will continue to do so.</i>


00:53:39.520 --> 00:53:44.760
<i>We will continue to fight
for our future and for the living planet.</i>


00:53:45.800 --> 00:53:49.028
We need to start
treating the crisis as a crisis.


00:53:49.040 --> 00:53:51.868
And we also need to communicate


00:53:51.880 --> 00:53:55.388
in a way that we connect
all these environmental disasters.


00:53:55.400 --> 00:53:59.348
Like everything from
acidification of the oceans, deforestation


00:53:59.360 --> 00:54:03.268
to the fact that we are in
the sixth mass extinction right now.


00:54:03.280 --> 00:54:06.348
We need to make sure the people
can connect these dots.


00:54:06.360 --> 00:54:10.908
Yeah. Absolutely. Connecting the dots,
that's a very good point.


00:54:10.920 --> 00:54:13.668
- Hi, Greta, it's a pleasure to meet you.
- You too.


00:54:13.680 --> 00:54:19.720
I wish you well and continue to campaign.
Just do what you believe is right.


00:54:20.480 --> 00:54:24.000
- Greta, can I have a selfie?
Is that okay?


00:54:25.480 --> 00:54:27.920
There we go. One, two, three!


00:54:31.360 --> 00:54:35.268
<i>Everyone says, "It's
so lovely that you are here,"</i>


00:54:35.280 --> 00:54:38.908
<i>and, "We promise to improve."</i>


00:54:38.920 --> 00:54:41.680
<i>But they never do.</i>


00:54:45.400 --> 00:54:48.148
<i>When I'm in these fancy environments,</i>


00:54:48.160 --> 00:54:52.308
<i>all these palaces or castles,
or whatever it is,</i>


00:54:52.320 --> 00:54:55.520
<i>I feel very uncomfortable.</i>


00:54:56.640 --> 00:55:01.388
<i>It feels like everyone is in
this role-playing game</i>


00:55:01.400 --> 00:55:03.600
<i>and just pretending.</i>


00:55:05.680 --> 00:55:07.680
<i>It feels kind of fake.</i>


00:55:13.040 --> 00:55:16.228
<i>Sometimes it feels like
it doesn't even matter</i>


00:55:16.240 --> 00:55:18.440
<i>how many of us go on strike.</i>


00:55:19.360 --> 00:55:23.668
<i>What matters is that
the emissions have to be reduced.</i>


00:55:23.680 --> 00:55:25.840
<i>And it has to start happen.</i>


00:57:46.800 --> 00:57:49.108
Let's be honest, a lot of people
find her very annoying.


00:57:49.120 --> 00:57:50.908
And they find her very hyperbolic


00:57:50.920 --> 00:57:53.160
and very hysterical
and very over-emotional.


00:57:53.840 --> 00:57:56.508
Greta. You know Greta?


00:58:10.880 --> 00:58:13.548
She's not the messiah.


00:58:13.560 --> 00:58:18.468
She's just a depressed
and extremely anxious girl.


00:58:18.480 --> 00:58:20.760
<i>And a very unhappy one.</i>


00:58:22.000 --> 00:58:24.628
<i>Asperger's is very rarely an advantage.</i>


00:58:24.640 --> 00:58:27.108
<i>In this case, it's actually a weakness.</i>


00:58:27.120 --> 00:58:29.708
<i>She's a kid. She talks nonsense.</i>


00:58:29.720 --> 00:58:34.068
<i>She tells the climate alarmists
exactly what they want to hear.</i>


00:58:34.080 --> 00:58:38.468
<i>You selfish, badly educated,
virtue-signaling little turds.</i>


00:58:38.480 --> 00:58:40.908
<i>Wake up, grow up, and shut up.</i>


00:58:40.920 --> 00:58:44.640
<i>Until you're sure of the facts
before protesting.</i>


01:00:51.720 --> 01:00:54.748
<i>My parents... I can tell</i>


01:00:54.760 --> 01:00:58.440
<i>that they are very worried,
and scared.</i>


01:01:01.680 --> 01:01:07.080
<i>We've received several letters home
that contain death threats.</i>


01:01:10.280 --> 01:01:13.960
<i>They're saying that
I should avoid going out.</i>


01:01:16.360 --> 01:01:19.080
<i>But I am honestly not that scared.</i>


01:01:20.560 --> 01:01:24.960
<i>Because I am more worried
what would happen if I didn't do this.</i>


01:01:30.640 --> 01:01:32.948
You're okay with
everything that's happening?


01:01:32.960 --> 01:01:38.028
Yeah. But I can't really plan my future.


01:01:38.040 --> 01:01:40.868
Like, I want to study that,


01:01:40.880 --> 01:01:44.268
and then I want to work there,
and I want to get married.


01:01:44.280 --> 01:01:46.788
I-I, I can't do...


01:01:46.800 --> 01:01:51.548
I can't even plan what I want to do this
weekend because someone calls and says,


01:01:51.560 --> 01:01:54.788
"Oh, we have an emergency meeting,"
and I have to go there.


01:01:54.800 --> 01:02:00.840
I mean, we don't
want to, like, burn out.


01:02:01.440 --> 01:02:03.908
If you understand, like...


01:02:03.920 --> 01:02:08.708
You don't have any energy left to
do something, you have used up your...


01:02:08.720 --> 01:02:13.068
- Yeah, I know what you mean.
I totally know what you mean.


01:02:13.080 --> 01:02:18.388
That's totally true. I think you should
especially be really careful for that.


01:02:18.400 --> 01:02:22.948
Yeah, we all should. We just have
to continue saying the same thing


01:02:22.960 --> 01:02:26.788
over and over again until people get it.


01:02:26.800 --> 01:02:30.320
- Yeah.
- Because if... yeah.


01:02:32.640 --> 01:02:34.280
Then we do that.


01:02:34.840 --> 01:02:37.548
So the whole area was forest.


01:02:37.560 --> 01:02:41.068
It was this ancient,
thousands of years old forest.


01:02:41.080 --> 01:02:45.268
And 90% of it was
lost to the coal mine.


01:02:45.280 --> 01:02:49.188
- There, on the horizon...
- Is the remaining ten percent.


01:02:49.200 --> 01:02:52.588
Yeah. This is our Hambach forest.


01:02:52.600 --> 01:02:55.428
It is very important because
this is such an important place,


01:02:55.440 --> 01:02:57.788
such a symbolic place.


01:02:57.800 --> 01:03:00.908
The Hambach forest is very threatened.


01:03:00.920 --> 01:03:04.508
And I felt like I wanted
to come here to visit that.


01:03:04.520 --> 01:03:10.560
And also to gain media attention
so that the media would focus on it.


01:03:14.200 --> 01:03:18.920
<i>Humanity sees nature
as this giant bag of candy.</i>


01:03:21.000 --> 01:03:23.920
<i>That we can just
take as much as we want.</i>


01:03:27.680 --> 01:03:32.360
<i>So one day, nature will
probably strike back in some way.</i>


01:03:35.640 --> 01:03:38.160
<i>I don't know exactly how.</i>


01:03:39.120 --> 01:03:42.588
<i>But there's everything
from heat waves to diseases,</i>


01:03:42.600 --> 01:03:46.560
<i>or water shortages,
which might become problems in the future.</i>


01:03:48.400 --> 01:03:51.480
<i>And in that context, we're kind of small.</i>


01:03:52.280 --> 01:03:54.908
<i>The Amazon
basin is burning at a record rate.</i>


01:03:54.920 --> 01:03:59.788
<i>More than 72,000 fires have
scorched the country this year,</i>


01:03:59.800 --> 01:04:04.908
<i>an over 80% increase
compared to the same period in 2018.</i>


01:04:04.920 --> 01:04:09.548
<i>Flames destroying one-and-a-half football
fields of rainforest every minute.</i>


01:04:09.560 --> 01:04:12.708
<i>Smoke spreading
across nearly half of Brazil</i>


01:04:12.720 --> 01:04:15.708
<i>visible from space
more than a week ago.</i>


01:04:15.720 --> 01:04:17.788
<i>Often called
"the lungs of the earth,"</i>


01:04:17.800 --> 01:04:21.628
<i>the rainforest supplies
20% of the world's oxygen.</i>


01:04:21.640 --> 01:04:26.388
<i>If it burns to a point of no return,
it could turn into a dry savannah</i>


01:04:26.400 --> 01:04:30.800
<i>plunging the planet ever deeper
into a climate change crisis.</i>


01:04:36.880 --> 01:04:41.760
I'm a Member of Parliament,
and I have a report I'd like to hand over.


01:04:48.520 --> 01:04:50.828
Smile for the cameras.


01:04:53.920 --> 01:04:58.108
- Thank you very much.
- My name is Greta Thunberg.


01:04:58.120 --> 01:05:02.628
I come from Sweden,
and I want you to panic.


01:05:02.640 --> 01:05:06.628
I want you to act as if
the house was on fire.


01:05:06.640 --> 01:05:10.108
I have said those words before.


01:05:10.120 --> 01:05:14.788
And a lot of people have
explained why that is a bad idea.


01:05:14.800 --> 01:05:18.388
And it's okay if you
refuse to listen to me.


01:05:18.400 --> 01:05:23.188
I am, after all, just
a 16-year-old schoolgirl from Sweden.


01:05:23.200 --> 01:05:25.600
But you cannot ignore the science.


01:05:27.880 --> 01:05:31.400
We are in the midst of
the sixth mass extinction.


01:05:33.760 --> 01:05:36.468
Erosion...


01:05:36.480 --> 01:05:40.640
of fertile topsoil, defo...


01:05:42.240 --> 01:05:48.188
Deforestation of our
great forests, toxic air pollution.


01:05:48.200 --> 01:05:51.948
The loss of insects and wildlife.


01:05:51.960 --> 01:05:55.388
The acidification of our oceans.


01:05:55.400 --> 01:06:01.428
These are all disastrous trends
being accelerated by a way of life that we


01:06:01.440 --> 01:06:04.788
here in our financially
fortunate part of the world


01:06:04.800 --> 01:06:07.748
see as our right
to simply carry on.


01:06:30.520 --> 01:06:33.188
Then you went
to the Strasbourg Parliament,


01:06:33.200 --> 01:06:37.868
and I saw you, during your speech, crying.


01:06:37.880 --> 01:06:43.348
- What made you cry?
- I talked about animals going extinct.


01:06:43.360 --> 01:06:48.588
Erosion, deforestation, acidification,
things like that, which is...


01:06:48.600 --> 01:06:52.988
I mean... It's hard to take in, but...


01:06:53.000 --> 01:06:56.748
And I talk about that
all the time, and once...


01:06:56.760 --> 01:07:01.640
I have to get emotional once,
it's only reasonable.


01:07:02.800 --> 01:07:07.628
- You suffer of Asperger's Syndrome.
Is this true?


01:07:07.640 --> 01:07:11.108
Yeah. Maybe I wouldn't say
"suffer from," but I have it.


01:07:11.120 --> 01:07:13.040
- You have it, okay.
- Yeah.


01:07:13.880 --> 01:07:17.748
Listen, Greta, in Italy,
we have talked a lot about you.


01:07:17.760 --> 01:07:23.428
And some people
describe you like a radical baby.


01:07:23.440 --> 01:07:27.628
You know, that...


01:07:42.760 --> 01:07:47.560
<i>Sometimes,
when they just sit and talk...</i>


01:07:48.920 --> 01:07:54.960
<i>I wonder to myself, "What would happen
if I just stood up and screamed here?"</i>


01:07:58.120 --> 01:08:03.148
<i>It feels like I'm speaking
a completely different language.</i>


01:08:03.160 --> 01:08:06.988
<i>Or as if the microphone isn't really on.</i>


01:08:07.000 --> 01:08:10.068
<i>...of all colleagues across the
House to welcome Greta Thunberg</i>


01:08:10.080 --> 01:08:15.348
<i>who is with us today, an enthusiastic
and dedicated environmental campaigner.</i>


01:08:20.440 --> 01:08:23.908
<i>Is the microphone on?</i>


01:08:23.920 --> 01:08:26.868
<i>Is the microphone really on?</i>


01:08:26.880 --> 01:08:29.788
<i>- Is my English okay?
- Yes!</i>


01:08:29.800 --> 01:08:32.348
<i>Because I'm beginning to wonder.</i>


01:08:34.240 --> 01:08:39.028
<i>You lied to us. You gave us false hope.</i>


01:08:39.040 --> 01:08:42.800
<i>You told us that the future
was something to look forward to.</i>


01:08:45.480 --> 01:08:48.708
<i>During the last six months,
I've traveled around Europe</i>


01:08:48.720 --> 01:08:52.428
<i>for hundreds of hours on trains,
electric cars and buses</i>


01:08:52.440 --> 01:08:57.668
<i>repeating these
life-changing words over and over again.</i>


01:08:57.680 --> 01:09:02.388
<i>But no one seems to be talking
about it and nothing has changed.</i>


01:09:02.400 --> 01:09:07.400
<i>Despite all the beautiful words
and promises, emissions are still rising.</i>


01:09:09.800 --> 01:09:13.228
<i>We have not taken to the streets
for you to take selfies with us</i>


01:09:13.240 --> 01:09:16.400
<i>and tell us that
you really admire what we do.</i>


01:09:17.520 --> 01:09:21.028
<i>We children are doing this
for you to put your differences aside</i>


01:09:21.040 --> 01:09:23.908
<i>and start acting as
you would in a crisis.</i>


01:09:23.920 --> 01:09:28.040
<i>We children are doing this because
we want our hopes and dreams back.</i>


01:09:31.080 --> 01:09:36.080
<i>I hope my microphone was on.
I hope you could all hear me. Thank you.</i>


01:10:06.120 --> 01:10:09.508
<i>In a few weeks, school will end.</i>


01:10:09.520 --> 01:10:14.508
<i>After the summer holidays,
I am starting gymnasium.</i>


01:10:14.520 --> 01:10:17.388
<i>It's like Swedish high school.</i>


01:10:17.400 --> 01:10:22.508
<i>And this is what I really
want to do because I love studying.</i>


01:10:22.520 --> 01:10:28.560
<i>But I have also been invited to attend the
United Nations Climate Summit in New York.</i>


01:10:29.840 --> 01:10:35.228
<i>And since time is running out,
I have decided to go there.</i>


01:10:42.840 --> 01:10:48.868
And since I don't fly because of
the enormous climate impact of aviation,


01:10:48.880 --> 01:10:50.708
it's going to be a challenge.


01:12:44.800 --> 01:12:48.548
- Greta! It's good, what you're doing.
- You too.


01:12:48.560 --> 01:12:51.548
Thanks, first of all, for your interest


01:12:51.560 --> 01:12:55.760
in our suggestion to sail over together.


01:12:56.560 --> 01:13:00.628
It may be a crazy idea,
but I really like it.


01:13:00.640 --> 01:13:04.428
And please, ask me any
question you want on the boat.


01:13:04.440 --> 01:13:09.908
I'll show you
around with the camera. Um, so...


01:13:09.920 --> 01:13:13.508
This, for example, is a bunk bed.


01:13:13.520 --> 01:13:19.108
A carbon fiber tube
with just a cloth on it.


01:13:19.120 --> 01:13:21.468
And a rope, where I can pull.


01:13:21.480 --> 01:13:25.320
It's a race boat for a small crew,
to, um...


01:13:26.680 --> 01:13:29.588
to be, uh, to be efficient.


01:13:29.600 --> 01:13:32.108
I'll show you the kitchen as well.


01:13:32.120 --> 01:13:35.800
- This is the kitchen.
- Ah-ha!


01:13:36.880 --> 01:13:40.348
And we heat water here.


01:13:40.360 --> 01:13:45.960
And then, this area here
we spend most of our time.


01:16:37.200 --> 01:16:39.628
<i>I don't want to be a person</i>


01:16:39.640 --> 01:16:42.720
<i>says one thing
and then does something else.</i>


01:16:45.120 --> 01:16:50.868
<i>I don't want to be the kind of person
who says, "This is so important"</i>


01:16:50.880 --> 01:16:56.480
<i>and then the next second, flies across
the world because it's easier that way.</i>


01:17:07.720 --> 01:17:10.708
<i>Many people would say this is crazy.</i>


01:17:10.720 --> 01:17:12.948
<i>Just take a flight.</i>


01:17:12.960 --> 01:17:15.988
Why do you not want to do that?


01:17:16.000 --> 01:17:18.268
Because by taking a boat,


01:17:18.280 --> 01:17:23.480
it shows that it's basically
impossible to live sustainable today.


01:17:47.680 --> 01:17:50.348
She faces a really,
really tough journey.


01:17:50.360 --> 01:17:53.628
I mean, it's an incredible boat.
It's fantastically exciting to sail.


01:17:53.640 --> 01:17:56.308
It's basically a huge sail
attached to a super-light hull.


01:17:56.320 --> 01:17:59.908
It leaps in the wind,
really muscular, jumps forward.


01:17:59.920 --> 01:18:02.988
What that means is,
that it crashes against the waves.


01:18:03.000 --> 01:18:06.068
Essentially, it's a giant drum
that bangs against the waves. As the...


01:18:06.080 --> 01:18:09.188
And then, here's a button.


01:18:09.200 --> 01:18:12.748
There's only one button,
so you will remember that.


01:18:12.760 --> 01:18:16.068
And this sends your GPS position...
This has a GPS.


01:18:16.080 --> 01:18:18.508
It sends it to a satellite.


01:18:18.520 --> 01:18:22.708
This is kind of
the worst-case scenario thing.


01:18:22.720 --> 01:18:27.308
It transmits for probably 24 hours
your position.


01:18:27.320 --> 01:18:30.468
The problem, why is it dangerous
to fall in the water?


01:18:30.480 --> 01:18:32.628
It's because you can get very cold.


01:18:32.640 --> 01:18:36.868
Um, the other thing is
to find you is difficult.


01:18:36.880 --> 01:18:41.028
For finding you,
this is one thing to have...


01:18:48.280 --> 01:18:51.160
- Greta, lots of love.
- Yeah, you too.


01:18:52.760 --> 01:18:57.028
- The UK strikers made you a video.
- Oh, thank you! Yeah.


01:18:59.760 --> 01:19:04.080
The whole world thinks
you're wonderful. Be a brave girl.


01:19:14.480 --> 01:19:20.160
Hip, hip, hooray! Hip, hip, hooray!


01:21:14.120 --> 01:21:17.068
And here the wind is
from behind, and light.


01:21:17.080 --> 01:21:21.828
Here's a high pressure.
This will be quite bumpy.


01:21:21.840 --> 01:21:25.348
And after that,
the wind is strong from behind.


01:21:25.360 --> 01:21:31.400
It starts to blow stronger at
five in the morning tomorrow morning.


01:21:32.840 --> 01:21:38.880
It will be a bit challenging,
but nothing dramatic, really.


01:27:54.160 --> 01:27:56.640
<i>Humans are social animals.</i>


01:27:57.880 --> 01:28:02.000
<i>And in a herd,
everyone has different roles.</i>


01:28:05.440 --> 01:28:09.360
<i>We are dependent
on each other to survive.</i>


01:28:23.120 --> 01:28:25.640
<i>If you see a threat...</i>


01:28:27.160 --> 01:28:30.120
<i>It's your responsibility
to sound the alarm.</i>


01:28:34.920 --> 01:28:39.760
<i>And I feel like this is
my responsibility, in a way.</i>


01:28:48.240 --> 01:28:51.548
<i>Excellencies, ladies and gentlemen,</i>


01:28:51.560 --> 01:28:55.080
<i>welcome to the 2019 Climate Action Summit.</i>


01:28:59.440 --> 01:29:03.560
<i>If I may ask you to
please take your seats.</i>


01:29:29.160 --> 01:29:31.588
<i>Greta, your first climate strike</i>


01:29:31.600 --> 01:29:34.268
<i>was a lonely event,
a little over a year ago</i>


01:29:34.280 --> 01:29:37.828
<i>demanding action for climate change.</i>


01:29:37.840 --> 01:29:40.800
<i>What's your message
to world leaders today?</i>


01:29:43.960 --> 01:29:49.148
This is all wrong.
I shouldn't be up here.


01:29:49.160 --> 01:29:53.828
I should be back in school,
on the other side of the ocean.


01:29:53.840 --> 01:29:58.348
Yet you all come to
us young people for hope.


01:29:58.360 --> 01:30:00.908
How dare you?


01:30:00.920 --> 01:30:06.388
You have stolen my dreams and
my childhood with your empty words.


01:30:06.400 --> 01:30:09.560
And, yet,
I'm one of the lucky ones.


01:30:10.400 --> 01:30:14.548
People are suffering.
People are dying.


01:30:14.560 --> 01:30:17.588
Entire ecosystems are collapsing


01:30:17.600 --> 01:30:23.640
and all you can talk about is money and
fairy tales of eternal economic growth.


01:30:24.040 --> 01:30:25.520
How dare you?


01:30:26.680 --> 01:30:31.000
For more than 30 years,
the science has been crystal clear.


01:30:31.960 --> 01:30:35.428
How dare you
continue to look away?


01:30:35.440 --> 01:30:38.508
And come here,
saying that you are doing enough?


01:30:38.520 --> 01:30:43.240
When the politics and solutions
needed are still nowhere in sight.


01:30:44.160 --> 01:30:46.668
You are failing us!


01:30:46.680 --> 01:30:51.588
But the young people are
starting to understand your betrayal.


01:30:51.600 --> 01:30:55.400
The eyes of all future
generations are upon you.


01:30:56.480 --> 01:31:01.760
And if you choose to fail us,
I say that we will never forgive you.


01:31:04.200 --> 01:31:06.948
<i>The world is waking up.</i>


01:31:06.960 --> 01:31:11.828
<i>And change is coming,
whether you like it or not.</i>


01:32:24.040 --> 01:32:28.960
<i>If you deal with crises in time,
instead of waiting...</i>


01:32:30.880 --> 01:32:33.040
<i>the problems won't get as big.</i>


01:32:40.840 --> 01:32:45.800
<i>Because if you do that,
you come out on the other side.</i>


01:32:48.640 --> 01:32:50.640
<i>And there, it's better.</i>


01:33:16.280 --> 01:33:21.280
<i>Actually, I don't see the world
in black and white.</i>


01:33:24.320 --> 01:33:28.520
<i>It's just the climate issue
I see in black and white.</i>


01:33:33.600 --> 01:33:38.080
<i>Sometimes I feel like it would be good
if everyone had a bit more Asperger's.</i>


01:33:41.840 --> 01:33:43.960
<i>At least when it comes to the climate.</i>


01:34:02.760 --> 01:34:07.480
<i>We, the youth,
say you are not doing enough!</i>


01:34:11.280 --> 01:34:16.720
We, the youth, demand action now!


01:34:20.720 --> 01:34:22.708
<i>We're on the outskirts</i>


01:34:22.720 --> 01:34:25.308
<i>of the biggest catastrophe
humanity has ever faced</i>


01:34:25.320 --> 01:34:28.160
and our
government is doing nothing!


01:34:29.560 --> 01:34:33.388
<i>Tell me why there are children
who have to stand up for themselves.</i>


01:34:33.400 --> 01:34:37.748
<i>Where are our parents,
where are our grandparents?</i>


01:34:37.760 --> 01:34:42.068
<i>We, as a human population,
need to be the change.</i>


01:34:42.080 --> 01:34:47.508
Because I will not sit and worry
about a future that I might not have!


01:34:47.520 --> 01:34:50.828
<i>Shout out, for
the sake of our environment.</i>


01:34:50.840 --> 01:34:54.200
And we, the younger generation,
we need to raise our voice.


01:35:10.080 --> 01:35:13.508
We have contaminated the Earth
and all the water,


01:35:13.520 --> 01:35:15.788
we have polluted the air.


01:35:15.800 --> 01:35:17.280
What have we done?

